Cross-check and discrepancies. DefiLlama's holder revenue and the on-chain burn valuation agree within about 0.5% since inception, 2–3% over 7 and 30 days, and about 6% over 90 days (on-chain higher; bridged burns arrive late, so windows are not aligned). They are independent methods: DL estimates fee × protocol share, while the author priced actual 0xdead inflows. Composition differs, however:

- DL v4 revenue is $0, but v4 fees are live. DL attributes all revenue to v3 and shows $0 for v4, even though on-chain the Ethereum PoolManager's protocolFeeController() is the V4FeeAdapter 0x89A5…051dB, and the TokenJar is receiving transfers from the PoolManager.

- DL v2 revenue is $0 for 30 days, but the v2 fee is on. v2 feeTo() is the TokenJar, which receives freshly minted UNI-V2 LP tokens.

- Likely explanations (author's inference): DL over-attributes to v3 and misses v4/v2; bridged L2 burns arrive at 0xdead about 7 days late; and searchers keep a margin.

Treat about $8M per 30 days as the current realized holder value, with ±10–15% uncertainty in any single month. Uniswap Labs stated on 2026-07-18 that protocol fees had "funded ~7.5M UNI (~$25.6M) of burn since December" ([thread 26162](https://gov.uniswap.org/t/temp-check-activate-v4-protocol-fees/26162)). The author's on-chain series gives 7.29M UNI arriving at 0xdead by 2026-07-18; the gap is consistent with the bridge lag.

Where burns come from (UNI to 0xdead since Dec 2025, by L1 sender; author's attribution):

- Direct Ethereum senders (Firepit callers, incl. an unverified searcher contract 0x331a…e1bc with 1.20M): 6.29M. The Ethereum Firepit nonce (1,546 × 4,000 UNI = 6.18M) explains most of it; the ~0.1M remainder was not attributed.

- Base L1StandardBridge 0x3154…2c35: 3.18M.

- A TransparentUpgradeableProxy 0x8500…6da0 whose implementation (0xf43b…0f02) is a verified Arbitrum-style L1ERC20Gateway: 2.70M. Likely the Robinhood Chain (Arbitrum Orbit) gateway; the chain is not confirmed.

- Arbitrum L1 ERC20 Gateway 0xa3a7…0eec: 1.11M.

- Wormhole NttManager 0x6569…0c44 (BNB/Polygon/Arc): 0.61M.

The largest single-day arrivals at 0xdead were 270K UNI on 2026-07-14 and 238K on 2026-06-16. The arrival date is not the same as the release date, because of bridge lag.

Not yet monetized / stated plans:

- PFDA (Protocol Fee Discount Auction), to auction fee-free swapping windows and burn the bids ([UNIfication](https://gov.uniswap.org/t/unification-proposal/25881)).

- Further v4 pool families and chains.

- UniswapX fees.

- Aggregator-hook fees: the family fee is set at 10 bp (3 bp on Base). The hooks went live 2026-10-22, so they barely show in the numbers yet.

