Limitation: the free public BSC RPC returns logs only for roughly the last 1.5 days and at most 50,000 blocks per query (older ranges return empty, 403 or "limit exceeded"), and Etherscan's free V2 API does not cover BSC (chainid 56 returns "Free API access is not supported for this chain", checked 2026-11-10). Individual old burn transactions can still be checked by receipt via bsc-dataseed.bnbchain.org (above). A full 30-day on-chain sum of buyback-burns therefore needs BscScan Pro, a paid RPC, or Dune ([dune.com/pancakeswap/PancakeSwap-CAKE-Tokenomics](https://dune.com/pancakeswap/PancakeSwap-CAKE-Tokenomics)). I did not do one. I cross-checked the dashboard series against the on-chain dead-address balance and the official monthly reports instead.

