### Key people

- Michael Egorov, founder of Curve (2020) and of Yield Basis (2025). X: [@newmichwill](https://x.com/newmichwill). He holds 27.2M CRV locked to 2030 at his known address and authors most Swiss Stake grant proposals. An analysis of his GitHub (Phemex, updated 2026-11-02) reports that through late October 2026 he wrote all 386 of the year's commits to Yield Basis core code and none of the 762 commits to Curve's stablecoin repository. His day-to-day engineering focus has shifted to Yield Basis, although Curve still quotes him as founder [17][11].

- Swiss Stake AG (Zug, Switzerland) is the company that builds and maintains Curve's code. It has about 25 contributors (per its grant proposal; not re-verified because the forum blocks automated access), funded by DAO CRV grants: 21M CRV for 2024–25; 17.45M CRV for 2026, first rejected 54.46% to 45.54% in Dec 2025 (on-chain CastVote events for vote 1286: Convex VoterProxy 308.8M and Yearn 82.9M veCRV against, i.e. 99.9% of the 391.9M "no" votes; StakeDAO 117.9M, part of Convex 108.5M and Egorov 26.1M voted for), then passed in an amended two-tranche form; plus a 520k crvUSD top-up in Apr 2026 [14][15]. A legal restructuring into a Swiss Association has been proposed [14]. No public CEO or C-suite titles are disclosed.

- Maximilian Roszko (X: [@MaxRoszko](https://x.com/MaxRoszko)) speaks publicly for Curve (Stable Summit, June 2026) [16]; his formal title was not confirmed.

- Charlie Watkins, an early core team member (Curve's second employee per the DefiLlama wiki) who proposed the original fee sharing with veCRV. His current role was not confirmed [21].

- Curve DAO, made up of veCRV holders. In practice it is dominated by Convex (54% of veCRV), StakeDAO (15%) and Yearn (11%). In August 2026 Convex moved its own gauge and DAO votes fully on-chain [7].

- Risk provider: yRisk (Yearn and Resupply contributors), selected Aug 2026 with 537M veCRV for and 0 against, and funded by vote 1492 (125k frxUSD + 568,181 CRV over 1 year) [7][15]. Departure: LlamaRisk, Curve's long-time risk provider, ended its engagement on 2026-06-30, and its unvested crvUSD stream was revoked (vote 1441) [16][15].

- Emergency DAO (eDAO): a multisig with limited emergency powers. It was given 400k crvUSD for peg defense (vote 1344, Feb 2026), and its scope was extended to Llamalend V2 (vote 1510, Oct 2026) [15][6].

- Official channels: X [@CurveFinance](https://x.com/CurveFinance); news [news.curve.finance](https://news.curve.finance/); forum [gov.curve.finance](https://gov.curve.finance/); docs [docs.curve.finance](https://docs.curve.finance/).

