#### Stated plan to monetise the token

There is none on record. Timeline: ZEIP-91 (2021) set protocol fees to $0 as a temporary experiment. In December 2021 the community concluded the experiment was "inconclusive" and recommended keeping $0. 0x Labs said it would "share initial thoughts" on new economics in early 2022 [11]. No ZEIP or 0x Labs proposal on token value accrual has been posted since. Community requests to "reinstate protocol fees" (2025-05-05) and a "Tokenomics" thread (2025-11-23) received no official reply on the forum [12]. Compare 1inch, KyberSwap and Jupiter, which have all run buyback programmes at some point.

### How to verify on-chain

All values below were obtained on 2026-11-10 (Ethereum block ~26,385,200–26,385,243) unless noted. Never put API keys into shared documents. Replace $KEY with your own Etherscan key.

#### 1. Supply and the two 0x-controlled wallets

# totalSupply() -> 0x...33b2e3c9fd0803ce8000000 = 1,000,000,000e18curl -s https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_call","params":[{"to":"0xE41d2489571d322189246DaFA5ebDE1F4699F498","data":"0x18160ddd"},"latest"]}'# balanceOf(Ext Dev Pool) -> 98,350,939.72 ZRX ; swap the address for Team Vesting 0xDB63D40C033D35E79CdbB21430f0FE10E9D97303 -> 53,252,497.37curl -s https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_call","params":[{"to":"0xE41d2489571d322189246DaFA5ebDE1F4699F498","data":"0x70a08231000000000000000000000000206376e8940E42538781cD94eF024Df3C1E0fD43"},"latest"]}'

Circulating = 1,000,000,000 − 98,350,939.72 − 53,252,497.37 = 848,396,562.91 ZRX, which matches CoinGecko exactly. Watch these two addresses for outflows, because that is the only material supply-side event possible.

#### 2. Is any fee reaching ZRX? (protocol fee multiplier)

# getProtocolFeeMultiplier() on 0x v4 Exchange Proxy -> 0x0 (= 0, fees off)curl -s https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com -H 'content-type: application/json' \ -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_call","params":[{"to":"0xDef1C0ded9bec7F1a1670819833240f027b25EfF","data":"0x487b5c20"},"latest"]}'

The selector 0x487b5c20 is keccak("getProtocolFeeMultiplier()")[0:4]. A non-zero value would mean ETH protocol fees resumed for v4 orders. Note that Settler swaps do not pay this fee in any case.

