Gross fees went from $114.8M in October 2025 to $39.7M in October 2026. Most of the decline is lower borrow demand and rates after the October 2025 crash and the April 2026 run. An independent analysis by Chado, via Odaily/KuCoin, measured DAO revenue of about $167K/day in the 144 days after the incident, against about $281K/day in the 144 days before, a 41% drop.

A note on figures: TokenLogic's budget ARFC (2026-03-04) puts 2025 DAO revenue at $142M and an "optimistic" 2026 operating budget at $190M, i.e. a structural deficit; DL's 2025 calendar-year protocol revenue is $124.98M (fact-checker's sum of DL daily data). Kulechov cited "$134M yearly revenue" in June 2026. The gap with DL most likely reflects revenue streams and accounting choices DL does not count (for example product/swap revenue). The exact reconciliation is not available.

#### Where the money goes

- Reserve factor. Interest accrues in each reserve as accruedToTreasury. Anyone can call Pool.mintToTreasury(assets[]), which mints aTokens to the Collector. Each mint emits Transfer(0x0 → Collector) on the aToken. The Ethereum Collector is [0x464C71f6c2F760DdA6093dCB91C24c39e5d6e18c](https://etherscan.io/address/0x464C71f6c2F760DdA6093dCB91C24c39e5d6e18c); each network has its own Collector.

- Liquidation protocol fee. The protocol's share of the liquidation bonus is transferred as aTokens directly to the Collector. The share was raised for WBTC, WETH and wstETH on V3 Ethereum Core in October 2026.

- GHO. 100% of GHO interest goes to the treasury.

- SVR and partner fees. Chainlink SVR (MEV recapture) and CoW Swap partner fees from the aave.com front-end are paid to the Collector. CoW pays weekly since 2026-04-23, per the DL methodology.

#### (c) What reaches AAVE holders: currently nothing

- Buyback program, 2025-04-09 to 2026-04-19.

- The DAO spent about $46.4M on AAVE (DL holders revenue; tokenbuybacks.app shows the same $46.4M but is built on DL data, so it is not an independent source — the independent check is the on-chain delivery log in section 8). By February 2026 it had bought more than 205,000 AAVE, 1.28% of supply ([TokenLogic Funding Insights](https://governance.aave.com/t/aave-dao-funding-insights/24192)).

- Execution: the Aave Finance Committee ran it with CoW Protocol orders. The settlement contract [0x9008D19f…ab41](https://etherscan.io/address/0x9008D19f58AAbD9eD0D60971565AA8510560ab41) delivered AAVE first to the AFC Safe [0x22740deB…1bFa](https://etherscan.io/address/0x22740deBa78d5a0c24C58C740e3715ec29de1bFa) and, from November 2025, to the Collector. The Collector then forwarded it to the AFC Safe.

- Tokens were not burned. On-chain, the AFC Safe supplied 220,308 AAVE into Aave V3 in May 2026 and another 20,194 in June 2026. It now holds 240,502 aEthAAVE (about $29.3M) and has borrowed 4,111,328 GHO against it, with a health factor of 5.42 (read via getUserAccountData at block 26,385,551, 2026-11-10 15:57 UTC; the draft's $30.38M / HF 5.62 at block 26,385,281 reflected the higher AAVE price an hour earlier).

- Last buy on-chain: the last CoW-settled AAVE delivery to the Collector was at 2026-04-19 14:00:47 UTC, 243.24 AAVE ([tx 0x566c6c3f…](https://etherscan.io/tx/0x566c6c3f083cbc8a8af942179e01f74437f2962f14c6b9cd8b37d2a501470ade)). None followed through block 26,385,281.

- The pause. It was formalized in the [\[ARFC\] Pause AAVE Buybacks](https://governance.aave.com/t/arfc-pause-aave-buybacks/24686) of 2026-04-22, "until the situation surrounding the rsETH incident becomes clearer". Before that, the [\[ARFC\] Buyback Program – Budget Adjustment](https://governance.aave.com/t/arfc-buyback-program-budget-adjustment/24229) (TokenLogic, 2026-03-04) cut the annual budget from about $50M to about $30M (about 292 AAVE/day) and switched the main funding source to ETH. It passed Snapshot on 2026-03-15 (363,253 for, 3,199 against). The pause ARFC passed Snapshot on 2026-05-01 (617,169 for, 4,893 against, 158,478 abstain; [Snapshot](https://snapshot.org/#/aavedao.eth)).

- Why it has not restarted: the rsETH balance-sheet hole.

- The DAO approved giving away 25,000 ETH, about $52M at today's price ([ARFC rsETH Incident Funding Update](https://governance.aave.com/t/arfc-rseth-incident-funding-update/24740)).

- It accepted a Mantle credit facility of up to 30,000 ETH. Reported terms are up to 36 months at the Lido staking yield plus 1% (Chado/Odaily via [KuCoin](https://www.kucoin.com/news/flash/aave-s-repurchase-stalled-473-days-needed-to-repay-loan)). These terms come from press, not from loan documents. The ARFC itself authorizes pledging DAO assets and future protocol revenue as collateral for recovery loans, without fixing amounts.

- At about $167K/day of DAO revenue, repaying a full 30,000 ETH facility would take about 473 days (Chado/Odaily, 2026-09-22).

- The amount actually drawn on the Mantle facility and repaid so far is not publicly reconciled. It is not available to the author.

- Stakers receive 150 AAVE/day from the Ecosystem Reserve. This is a transfer of existing treasury AAVE, not a distribution of fee revenue.

#### Stated plan to restore value capture

- Aavenomics 3.0: "immutable and automated buybacks of AAVE" (Kulechov on X, 2026-06-25, quoted on the [forum](https://governance.aave.com/t/restart-aave-buy-backs/24936)). On 2026-09-28 he added "We're considering also burn". As of 2026-11-10 there is no ARFC, budget, ratio or date. A community ARFC on 2026-10-23 questions whether staking should play any role in it ([forum](https://governance.aave.com/t/arfc-staking-in-aavenomics-3-0-do-we-want-it/25905)).

- "Aave Will Win" (TEMP CHECK Snapshot 2026-02-28: 622,256 YAE vs 497,050 NAY; ARFC Snapshot closed 2026-04-04: 727,572 for vs 174,330 against; binding on-chain vote reported passed 2026-04-12 with 522,780 for and 175,310 against per The Block — the on-chain tally was not re-read by the fact-checker). 100% of revenue from Aave-branded products goes to the DAO: the aave.com swap integration (about $10M/yr claimed in February 2026), the App, Card, Pro, Kit, Horizon and the ETP. In exchange, Aave Labs gets $25M in stablecoins plus 75,000 AAVE.

- V4 monetization: the Risk Premium, curator revenue share (50% of the Sentora instance) and a proposed "reinvestment module" for idle liquidity.

- Babylon BTC spokes: TokenPost reports that the DAO takes the first $500K/yr, and that 4–7% of revenue goes to repurchasing AAVE and BABY. This comes from secondary reporting; the ARFC text should be checked.

### How to verify on-chain

All values below were read by the author at Ethereum block 26,385,281 (2026-11-10 15:02:59 UTC). Use any public RPC. Etherscan calls need your own key in $ETHERSCAN_API_KEY.

#### 1. Supply and treasury AAVE

# AAVE totalSupply -> 0x...d3c21bcecceda1000000 = 16,000,000e18curl -s https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_call","params":[{"to":"0x7Fc66500c84A76Ad7e9c93437bFc5Ac33E2DDaE9","data":"0x18160ddd"},"latest"]}'# AAVE balanceOf(Ecosystem Reserve 0x25F2226B597E8F9514B3F68F00f494cF4f286491) -> 559,284.95 AAVEcurl -s https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_call","params":[{"to":"0x7Fc66500c84A76Ad7e9c93437bFc5Ac33E2DDaE9","data":"0x70a0823100000000000000000000000025f2226b597e8f9514b3f68f00f494cf4f286491"},"latest"]}'# stkAAVE totalSupply -> 2,456,488 stkAAVE at block 26,385,551 (1:1 with AAVE; getExchangeRate() 0xe6aa216c -> 1e18)curl -s https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com -H 'content-type: application/json' -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"eth_call","params":[{"to":"0x4da27a545c0c5B758a6BA100e3a049001de870f5","data":"0x18160ddd"},"latest"]}'

