The healthy-vault run-rate ($5.66M/yr) is consistent with DefiLlama's 30d annualized $6.6M. The stuck vaults are Plasma $109.9M, Avalanche $33.7M (mainly eUSDt-3 at 30% APR), Ethereum $29.7M (eUSDC-64, eWBTC-9, eWETH-33, eUSDC-47) and Sonic $22.6M (69–139% APR). They accrue interest that cannot be paid out because the vaults hold no cash. They are consistent with the Stream Finance (November 2025) and Resolv (March 2026) collateral failures described by Euler Labs. Classifying ≥99% utilization as "stuck" is my estimate, not an official Euler designation. Monad accounts for $91.5M (72%) of healthy borrowing.

