Why the sources differ: Datum found that DefiLlama's adapter overstates fees by 14.5% and revenue by 38.5% on overlapping August days. The adapter multiplies per-share growth by total assets instead of total shares. The adapter also had a gap after 2026-08-22 (per Datum). DefiLlama has since backfilled 2026-08-23 → 09-02, but the backfilled days read $71–78K/day of fees versus $36–45K/day just before (DefiLlama dailyFees series, queried 2026-11-10), so treat late-August/early-September DefiLlama figures as unreliable. DefiLlama counts accrued protocol fees, while Datum counts what was converted. My scan shows the healthy-vault protocol share is near zero (~$2.2K/yr). The remaining nominal accrual sits in stuck vaults with per-vault 50–100% protocol overrides. On-chain, these are 9 Ethereum vaults with SetFeeConfigSetting 50% overrides dated 2025-11-13 and 2025-11-27, plus Avalanche and Sonic vaults showing protocolFeeShare()=5000.

