Ethereum monthly EUL bought via Fee Flow (on-chain Buy events):

- 2025: Sep 27,945; Oct 22,735; Nov 39,530; Dec 27,587

- 2026: Jan 36,157; Feb 90,534; Mar 81,084; Apr 41,704

- The last purchase was 19,714.91 EUL on 2026-04-11 02:40 UTC (tx 0x68429b66…bb32bc56).

Mechanism, exactly: vault convertFees() mints fee shares to the curator's feeReceiver and the protocol's receiver from ProtocolConfig.protocolFeeConfig(vault). The protocol receiver is the FeeFlowController when Fee Flow is on, or the DAO multisig when it is off. FeeFlowController buy(assets, assetsReceiver, epochId, deadline, maxPayment) transfers EUL from the buyer to paymentReceiver (= 0xcAD001…1DCe) and sends the inventory to the buyer.

- Bought EUL was not burned or distributed. It accumulated in DAO multisigs. Since 2025-11-12 the Operational multisig received 303,798 EUL from feeFlowControllerUtil and 282,916 EUL bridged from other chains via the OFT adapter. It sent 3,408,490 EUL to the Treasury on 2025-11-12 and 692,381 EUL to Safe 0x0e33 on 2026-10-02.

- Even when it was active, holder value accrual was indirect: buy pressure plus treasury accumulation.

Current state: protocol fees are 0% by default on all checked chains, and Fee Flow is paused. The docs say "Euler does not currently charge protocol fees". The stated plan to monetize comes from the Q1 2026 retrospective and the 2026-04-29 proposal: "growth must come before monetization". The DAO "retain[s] the ability to reintroduce protocol fees through a future governance proposal". Labs also announced a protocol upgrade so the DAO can enforce a minimum fee on existing vaults later. No threshold, metric or date for reintroduction has been published. Euler Labs says it "has sufficient runway" but publishes no financials.

