Sum on these chains (Arbitrum USDY 0x35e050d3C0eC2d29D269a8EcEa763a183bDF9A9D, Mantle 0x5bE26527e817998A7206475496fDE1E68957c5A6): 2,063.5M USDY × $1.15268 = $2.379B. That matches the Ondo site TVL of $2.39B and CG's $2.393B. Sui, Aptos, Noble, Tempo and Plume were not read. Ondo's own portfolio report says "USDY outstanding $1.97B" (2026-11-06). The roughly $0.4B gap from on-chain supply is not explained by Ondo. Two facts are relevant: the top two Ethereum holders are unlabelled Safes holding 359.0M (0xa5b6…5302) and 298.8M (0x661b…ee1a) USDY (Ethplorer, re-checked), and Ondo's footnote 5 says the collateralization ratio "excludes US Treasury securities used for structured financing". Note that Ondo's own two figures give $2.42B / $1.97B = 122.9%, not the 156.90% printed, so the printed ratio uses a different (unstated) numerator/denominator. Against on-chain supply, underlying assets of $2.42B are about 102%.

