Mechanism exactly: none. The token contract has no fee hooks. (Context from the FY2025 accounts, note 16: contract liabilities — licence/service fees paid in advance — had £12,000,000 of additions and £11,494,031 released to revenue in FY2025; these are fiat prepayments, with no reference to QNT anywhere in the 38-page filing.) The only documented holder-value channel — licence-driven purchase and 12-month lock of QNT through the Overledger treasury contracts — shows zero on-chain activity since deployment on 2020-06-30 and was officially superseded by Fusion (repo archived 2026-02-06). If Quant buys/locks QNT off-chain or in undisclosed wallets, it cannot be verified.

Stated plan to monetise via the token: Overledger/Fusion docs (2026) describe QNT staking against nodes "to earn rewards and unlock higher capacity tiers" and QNT as an accepted payment token for Flow App x402 gates. No dates, fee rates, reward rates, or a fee-to-QNT conversion rule have been published in the docs read for this report.

